    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1489">

                <pb facs="1197" n="1081" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1081"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.51/294.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 161.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Managua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-12-30">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 30, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose herewith a
                    copy and translation of a Presidential decree,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1489-f1"/>
                    which was subsequently ratified by the Assembly, approving the transaction
                    entered into by Messers Brown Bros, and Co. and J. and W. Seligman and Co., as
                    authorized agents of the Republic of Nicaragua with the Ethelburga Syndicate
                    Ltd, <pb facs="1198" n="1082" xml:id="pg1082"/> of London. This decree bears
                    date of the 14th instant, and was published in the “Gaceta Oficial” on the 23rd
                    instant.</p>
                <p>The President and other members of his Government have expressed to me their
                    gratification at this prompt and satisfactory solution of this harassing and
                    disturbing obligation.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">F. M. Gunther.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
